{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "8244716",
      "title": "Consuming the Context",
      "sourceHash": "fc0e10d493a5779ae10f5b4367ad396ea90aae24eb6861e77d5593145c9dcbb2",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.87,
          "end": 3.48,
          "en": "So now that we're providing the context,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.48,
          "end": 5.37,
          "en": "let's consume it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.37,
          "end": 8.943,
          "en": "And we could, for example, consume it in the Cart component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.87,
          "end": 12.54,
          "en": "because there I need the Cart items,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.54,
          "end": 16.65,
          "en": "which is why currently I'm getting them through props,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.65,
          "end": 19.2,
          "en": "so that those items can be output here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.2,
          "end": 21.54,
          "en": "or this fallback text here can be shown",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.54,
          "end": 23.493,
          "en": "if we have no items in the cart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.66,
          "end": 27.57,
          "en": "Now that we added this context feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.57,
          "end": 30.75,
          "en": "and this context we created here has a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.75,
          "end": 35.01,
          "en": "that does have an, at the moment, empty items array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.01,
          "end": 37.92,
          "en": "we can and should consume this context",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.92,
          "end": 39.573,
          "en": "to get hold of these items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.47,
          "end": 41.79,
          "en": "And we'll soon make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.79,
          "end": 44.883,
          "en": "that those items aren't always empty, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.05,
          "end": 51.05,
          "en": "Now to do that, we must import this CartContext",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.44,
          "end": 54.84,
          "en": "from our store folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.84,
          "end": 58.68,
          "en": "and there the shopping-cart-context.jsx file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.68,
          "end": 61.14,
          "en": "And then here in this file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.14,
          "end": 64.62,
          "en": "where we're also importing CartContext,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.62,
          "end": 67.26,
          "en": "so where we want to access this context,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.26,
          "end": 71.76,
          "en": "we also have to import something from react",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.76,
          "end": 75.72,
          "en": "and that something is one of two hooks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.72,
          "end": 79.47,
          "en": "that help us with getting hold of that context.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.47,
          "end": 83.40299999999999,
          "en": "And the first hook we can use is the useContext hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 84.27,
          "end": 86.34,
          "en": "This hook does what the name implies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.34,
          "end": 89.37,
          "en": "You can use it to consume some context",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 89.37,
          "end": 93.84,
          "en": "or to access some context from inside a component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 93.84,
          "end": 96.3,
          "en": "And you would use this hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 96.3,
          "end": 99.093,
          "en": "by calling it inside of the component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 100.02000000000001,
          "end": 102.99000000000001,
          "en": "And by then passing this context object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102.99000000000001,
          "end": 106.68299999999999,
          "en": "this CartContext in this case, to it as an argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 108.24000000000001,
          "end": 111.99000000000001,
          "en": "And you'll get back a value from useContext,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 111.99000000000001,
          "end": 114.96000000000001,
          "en": "which you can store in a constant or a variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 114.96000000000001,
          "end": 118.593,
          "en": "Here I'll store it in a constant called cartCtx.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 119.49000000000001,
          "end": 121.05,
          "en": "And that will be the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 121.05,
          "end": 123.51,
          "en": "that is in the end provided by this context",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 123.51,
          "end": 125.58,
          "en": "and we'll work with that value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 125.58,
          "end": 127.68299999999999,
          "en": "throughout the next minutes and lectures.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 128.94,
          "end": 133.56,
          "en": "But that's just one way of getting hold of the context.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 133.56,
          "end": 136.53,
          "en": "There also is another hook you could use instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 136.53,
          "end": 139.44,
          "en": "and that would be the use hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 139.44,
          "end": 142.68,
          "en": "So it's just called use, nothing else,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 142.68,
          "end": 146.37,
          "en": "and you would use it like the useContext hook, essentially.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 146.37,
          "end": 150.06,
          "en": "So it's shorter, but besides that, it is used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 150.06,
          "end": 151.923,
          "en": "in pretty much the same way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 152.76,
          "end": 155.76,
          "en": "And indeed, it will also give you that context value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 155.76,
          "end": 158.7,
          "en": "as a return value and you can therefore then use it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 158.7,
          "end": 160.05,
          "en": "as I'm using it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 160.05,
          "end": 162.69299999999998,
          "en": "In this case, I'm storing it in a constant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 164.13,
          "end": 168.21,
          "en": "Now why do we have two hooks for the same purpose?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 168.21,
          "end": 171.87,
          "en": "Well, the use hook is a bit more flexible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 171.87,
          "end": 174.03,
          "en": "than the useContext hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 174.03,
          "end": 177.18,
          "en": "Because the use hook, whilst it is a React hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 177.18,
          "end": 180.96,
          "en": "and whilst it can only be used in React components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 180.96,
          "end": 184.59,
          "en": "or other hooks, can for example be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 184.59,
          "end": 187.29,
          "en": "inside of an if block.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 187.29,
          "end": 192.093,
          "en": "So this code here would be valid when using the use hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 193.23,
          "end": 197.34,
          "en": "Now normally, you're not allowed to use React hooks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 197.34,
          "end": 200.04,
          "en": "in if blocks or for loops.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 200.04,
          "end": 201.57,
          "en": "So normally, this would not work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 201.57,
          "end": 203.37,
          "en": "but with the use hook, it will work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 203.37,
          "end": 205.62,
          "en": "So whenever you have a situation like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 205.62,
          "end": 209.49,
          "en": "you could simply use the use hook to have valid code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 209.49,
          "end": 214.47,
          "en": "If you were using useContext, this would not be allowed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 214.47,
          "end": 217.833,
          "en": "This would be an incorrect way of using a React hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 218.67000000000002,
          "end": 222.03,
          "en": "And of course, useContext is a bit longer than use,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 222.03,
          "end": 225,
          "en": "so using the use hook simply is a bit more convenient,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 225,
          "end": 226.47,
          "en": "you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 226.47,
          "end": 229.68,
          "en": "But the use hook is only available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 229.68,
          "end": 233.88,
          "en": "if you're using React version 19 or higher.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 233.88,
          "end": 238.88,
          "en": "In older React versions, like React 18, it's not available.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 239.04,
          "end": 241.85,
          "en": "There, you have to use useContext.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 243.39,
          "end": 246.3,
          "en": "And therefore, since I want to show you code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 246.3,
          "end": 248.19,
          "en": "that is backwards compatible,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 248.19,
          "end": 251.67,
          "en": "so that would also work with older React versions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 251.67,
          "end": 253.17,
          "en": "and since I don't need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 253.17,
          "end": 257.19,
          "en": "to access my context conditionally here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 257.19,
          "end": 260.94,
          "en": "I will use useContext instead of use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 260.94,
          "end": 264.99,
          "en": "And by the way, the useContext hook is also still available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 264.99,
          "end": 268.32,
          "en": "if you are using React 19 or higher.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 268.32,
          "end": 272.43,
          "en": "So you can use that hook without problems there as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 272.43,
          "end": 274.47,
          "en": "I just mentioned the use hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 274.47,
          "end": 277.2,
          "en": "so that you are aware of this alternative",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 277.2,
          "end": 278.73,
          "en": "and of course, you could use it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 278.73,
          "end": 282.21,
          "en": "if you are using at least React version 19.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 282.21,
          "end": 285.81,
          "en": "But here in this course for backwards compatibility reasons,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 285.81,
          "end": 288.213,
          "en": "I'll use the useContext hook instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 289.35,
          "end": 294.3,
          "en": "And therefore, this value should have a items property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 294.3,
          "end": 297,
          "en": "because we added a items property here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 297,
          "end": 298.653,
          "en": "in this initial value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 300.03,
          "end": 303.527,
          "en": "Hence, we cannot use CartContext here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 303.527,
          "end": 308.527,
          "en": "and use cart context, or cartCtx, as I named it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 308.947,
          "end": 311.673,
          "en": ".items.length here in this check.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 312.54,
          "end": 316.233,
          "en": "And then do the same here for this second check.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 317.19,
          "end": 321.33,
          "en": "And then also use cartCtx.items here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 321.33,
          "end": 323.613,
          "en": "when we map through these items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 325.41,
          "end": 328.35,
          "en": "So that we're no longer using this prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 328.35,
          "end": 330.66,
          "en": "and we therefore can get rid of that prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 330.66,
          "end": 332.073,
          "en": "and we should get rid of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 333.18,
          "end": 336.99,
          "en": "And also use cartCtx.items up here therefore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 336.99,
          "end": 340.923,
          "en": "where I basically derive the totalPrice from those items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 343.17,
          "end": 347.853,
          "en": "And with that, if we save this, we'll get an empty website.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 348.99,
          "end": 353.17,
          "en": "And we can see why it's empty if we open the developer tools",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 354.6,
          "end": 356.19,
          "en": "because here we learn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 356.19,
          "end": 360.99,
          "en": "that we did not add the required value prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 360.99,
          "end": 363.513,
          "en": "to our Context.Provider component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 365.22,
          "end": 368.73,
          "en": "And that's indeed one thing we also have to do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 368.73,
          "end": 372,
          "en": "Even though we're setting a default value here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 372,
          "end": 375.12,
          "en": "you also must add a value prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 375.12,
          "end": 377.943,
          "en": "to your CartContext.Provider component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 380.16,
          "end": 383.91,
          "en": "And here I'll set the value prop to an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 383.91,
          "end": 386.613,
          "en": "that also has such an empty items array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 387.69,
          "end": 390.48,
          "en": "So we do need to set that value prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 390.48,
          "end": 394.44,
          "en": "and also provide our context value here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 394.44,
          "end": 398.07,
          "en": "And I'll get back to why this default value here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 398.07,
          "end": 401.253,
          "en": "can still be useful, in a couple of seconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 402.48,
          "end": 404.64,
          "en": "But you need to add this value prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 404.64,
          "end": 408.33,
          "en": "and provide your context value here as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 408.33,
          "end": 412.08,
          "en": "in this case, as a dynamic kind of hard-coded value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 412.08,
          "end": 412.923,
          "en": "at the moment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 413.88,
          "end": 416.28,
          "en": "And if you now save that, you'll see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 416.28,
          "end": 418.17,
          "en": "that the website is there again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 418.17,
          "end": 420.57,
          "en": "And if I now open the cart,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 420.57,
          "end": 422.71,
          "en": "I get no items in the cart",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 424.38,
          "end": 426.22,
          "en": "and I got no error here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 427.17,
          "end": 431.13,
          "en": "and this now proves that this context feature is working",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 431.13,
          "end": 434.52,
          "en": "because I'm getting this no items in cart message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 434.52,
          "end": 438.69,
          "en": "because at the moment, my context items, of course, always",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 438.69,
          "end": 440.073,
          "en": "is an empty array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 441.21,
          "end": 443.58,
          "en": "But I'm not getting an error or anything else",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 443.58,
          "end": 445.56,
          "en": "and therefore, we can clearly see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 445.56,
          "end": 448.83299999999997,
          "en": "that we are able to read this context value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 450.63,
          "end": 454.77,
          "en": "Now why is setting this default value here useful?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
